  - line: 123
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 2: THE MAGES' GUILD — ONE BUILDING, TWO REALITIES"
  - line: 125
    type: narration
    text: "At the center of the vast, geometric stone circle stood… nothing."
  - line: 127
    type: narration
    text: "And everything."
  - line: 129
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt felt it first—a resonant tug behind his ribs, a sympathetic vibration from the dragon-scale armor."
  - line: 130
    type: narration
    text: "The plates warmed, and a low, harmonic hum filled his skull, a duet between Zaron's ancient consciousness and the latent magic of this place."
  - line: 131
    type: narration
    text: "Where his eyes saw empty crater floor, his perception saw a spiraling tower of woven light and solidified shadow, piercing the star-flecked blackness."
  - line: 133
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"There,\""
  - line: 135
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh stood beside him, her head tilted."
  - line: 136
    type: narration
    text: "\"I do not see it."
  - line: 137
    type: narration
    text: "But I feel its… seam."
  - line: 138
    type: narration
    text: "A fold in reality where the threads of cause and effect are braided loosely."
  - line: 139
    type: narration
    text: "It is a threshold.\""
  - line: 141
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck stared at the same empty space."
  - line: 142
    type: narration
    text: "His predator's eyes, capable of tracking heat and motion across miles, saw only ancient rock and their own footprints."
  - line: 143
    type: narration
    text: "He stepped forward, reached out a massive clawed hand, and swiped it through the air where the tower's entrance should be."
  - line: 144
    type: narration
    text: "His hand met no resistance."
  - line: 146
    type: narration
    text: "He withdrew it, looking at his empty claws, then at Geralt."
  - line: 147
    type: narration
    text: "There was no anger in his vertical-pupiled gaze."
  - line: 148
    type: narration
    text: "Only a deep, weary understanding."
  - line: 150
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"This is not my war,\""
  - line: 152
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt turned to him."
  - line: 153
    type: narration
    text: "\"Oreck—\""
  - line: 155
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I will not wait idly,\""
  - line: 156
    type: narration
    text: "the reptilian interrupted, his voice firm. \"This is Orion territory. Quiet, but not dead. I will scout the perimeter. Identify outposts. Guard your blind side.\" He placed a heavy hand on Geralt's armored shoulder. \"Protection sometimes means clearing the field so the mage can work. Do what you must learn. I will ensure you have the time to do it.\""
  - line: 158
    type: narration
    text: "With a final nod to Kyh, Oreck turned and loped away, his form soon blending into the monochrome landscape, a warrior purposefully stepping out of a story he could not read."
  - line: 160
    type: narration
    text: "The Guild isn't a place."
  - line: 161
    type: narration
    text: "It's a state of attunement."
  - line: 162
    type: narration
    text: "You don't enter it—you become worthy of it."
  - line: 164
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt and Kyh stepped forward together."
  - line: 165
    type: narration
    text: "As they crossed an invisible boundary, the Moon vanished."
  - line: 167
    type: narration
    text: "They stood in an atrium of impossible geometry."
  - line: 168
    type: narration
    text: "A central spiral staircase, seemingly carved from condensed starlight and the memory of obsidian, wound up into a ceiling that displayed not rock, but a swirling nebula."
  - line: 169
    type: narration
    text: "The air thrummed with a low-frequency pulse—the sound of time pooling."
  - line: 170
    type: narration
    text: "Luminescent orbs drifted like slow thoughts."
  - line: 171
    type: narration
    text: "It was silent, yet full of a pressure that spoke of concentrated thought spanning millennia."
  - line: 173
    type: narration
    text: "This was the Mages' Guild."
  - line: 174
    type: narration
    text: "The same building that existed in a forgotten valley on Earth, accessible only from places of power."
  - line: 175
    type: narration
    text: "Location was irrelevant."
  - line: 176
    type: narration
    text: "Only resonance mattered."
  - line: 178
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh gasped, her shadow-form trembling."
  - line: 179
    type: narration
    text: "\"The weave here… it is not meant for manipulation."
  - line: 180
    type: narration
    text: "It is a library."
  - line: 181
    type: narration
    text: "A living library of outcomes.\" She was already drawn toward an archway pulsing with deep blues and blacks, the Archive of Unlight."
  - line: 182
    type: narration
    text: "\"I must understand…\""
  - line: 184
    type: narration
    text: "She moved away, leaving Geralt alone in the humming stillness."
  - line: 186
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"

